# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the agent test binaries (docs/23 memory ladder, docs/12).
# GLib, GObject, GStreamer, libnice and libsoup are not built with TSan: their mutexes and
# atomics are invisible to it, so every hand-off through their queues (thread pools, idle
# sources, bus messages, pad probes) is reported as a race between the two ends. The
# kit's own hand-offs carry an acquire/release pair (glib::handoff_*), so what is left
# is the libraries' internal traffic, matched here by module name. A race with both ends
# in fjarr code has no frame in these modules and is never suppressed.
# (`called_from_lib` is deliberately not used: it refuses wildcards that match more
# than one library and aborts the process.)
race:libglib-2.0.so*
race:libgobject-2.0.so*
race:libgio-2.0.so*
race:libgmodule-2.0.so*
race:libgst*.so*
race:libnice.so*
race:libgupnp-igd-*.so*
race:libsoup-3.0.so*
race:libsrtp2.so*
race:libusrsctp.so*
